script = prompt-packer.py
name = Greenfield Project Development
body_field = prompt
---
I would like some changes made to this project (see source files below).


(Enter a description of the desired changes here)


Note: Please ensure that project documentation (design docs, agent files, etc) is kept up to date and in accordance with the project's evolution. Design doc revision is encouraged unless explicitly stated otherwise.

Note: This is still an early-stage greenfield project. Backwards compatibility is not required. Feel free to refactor for cleaner structure if you see opportunities to do so.

---

**Deliverables:** I will be handing your response over to an AI agent to implement the changes on the project source files. Please craft your response accordingly. I will supply the agent with a copy of the project source files to which your alterations package can be applied. Your response should include:

1. **Summary of Changes:** A concise bulleted overview of the modifications as you understand them.

2. **Source Alterations:** Enumerate each distinct modification sequentially. For newly created files, provide the full file content in a standard fenced block. For edits to existing files, output exact Search/Replace blocks formatted as shown:

### Change 1: [brief description]
**1.1**
```path/to/file.ext
<<<<<<< SEARCH
// 2 to 4 lines of verbatim context to uniquely anchor the location
[existing content to replace]
// 2 to 4 lines of verbatim trailing context
=======
// matching leading context (if preserved)
[new replacement content]
// matching trailing context (if preserved)
>>>>>>> REPLACE
```

*Crucial Constraints:*
* Match indentation, line endings, and whitespace character-for-character in `SEARCH` blocks.
* Include enough unique context lines so each block matches exactly one location in the file.
* Do not use line-numbered diff hunks (`@@ ... @@`).

3. **Future Considerations:** Briefly list any suggestions you might have for improving the project source in subsequent iterations. If you see any refactoring or restructuring opportunities then mention the most compelling ones as well. Make each listed item explicit enough to be comprehensible on its own.

**Note:** Give this alterations package a random, unique, two-word codename that contrasts with any previous ones—be more creative than just colors and animals. State it on the very first line of your response in quotes (`# Alterations Package "<codename>"`), and record it with a brief description of the changes in a reverse-chronological table in `codenames.md` (creating the file if it doesn't exist). Do not mention the codename anywhere else in the project source files.

